A||||4||87FieroGTx||Load webpages a LOT faster!!!||||1||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||08-04-2001||01:17 PM|||| I know this shouls be in O/T but everyone needs to see this it works SO GOOD!!<P> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR> I added thes to my registry and OMFG it works. It really works. This wont help as much on a 56K connection, but if you have Broadband (DSL-Cable-etc.) you will definately notice the difference. <P>On 56k It takes about 12 seconds to load a page On my DSL it used to take about 2 seconds. After I followed this advise, I tried again. Now it only takes me about .25 seconds. You will litterally miss the load time if you blink. If you have any questions about this ask. I will try to be as helpfull as I can. <P>AS ALWAYS....Save your registry to a backup before you do this.<P><BR>Load Web Pages Faster <BR>Increase Web page loading speed by doubling the number of possible concurrent open connections. Imagine a web page has 20 images and some text. In order for your browser to get all these files, it opens 2 or 4 concurrent connections, depending on the Web server. Increasing the number of open connections allows for faster retrieving of the data. <P>On Windows 9x/Me set or add these dword registry values under this key: <P>HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings Connection.<BR>MaxConnectionsPer1_0Server=00000020<BR>MaxConnectionsPerServer=00000010<P>On Windows NT/2K set or add these dword registry values:<P>MaxConnectionsPer1_0Server=00000020<BR>MaxConnectionsPerServer=00000020<P>under the above key as well as this key: <P>HKEY_USERS\.DEFAULT\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings. <P>This wasn't as simple as I expected to do since the instructions are a little obscure. SO .. I will try to explain it a little better.<P>*****************************************<BR>To do this click Start-Run and type 'regedit" and hit ok.<BR>You will see the registry editor. Click on each tree selection to expand to the next level.<BR>First Click "HKCU"<BR>Then "Software"<BR>Then "Microsoft" etc..until you get to <BR>HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings Connection<P>Once there Click on the edit menu and select "New" - "DWORD"<BR>A new entry will be made with a blinking cursor to edit the value.<P>Input the following text as the entry:<BR>MaxConnectionsPer1_0Server=00000020<P>then add another "DWORD" with the following test<BR>MaxConnectionsPerServer=00000010 <P>Once completed your set. I didnt have to reboot for the changes to take effect but if this doesnt immediately work you may want to do so. I will say you must restart Internet explorer befor youll notice and Close it before you start anyway.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 87FieroGTx (edited 08-04-2001).]||||reg||1
